From e846daa8d474c7a2ac37d4faa145dea9bfcd4e66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:09:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix getimagesize() returning uninitialised heap memory in
 $imageinfo (CVE-2025-14177)

php_read_APP() accepted any read of an APPn segment that returned more
than 0 bytes. When the stream returned fewer bytes than the segment
length (a truncated file, or a large segment read from a stream that
returns it in chunks), the rest of the buffer was uninitialised heap
memory, and getimagesize() returned it to the script in $imageinfo
(read for example by WordPress for IPTC data). The read must now return
the whole segment. An empty APP segment, which used to make
getimagesize() fail, is now returned as an empty string.

This is php-src ae04110032 (bug #71848, Christoph M. Becker), which 7.x
already has; same change as Sury's 5.6 patch 0287. GHSA-3237-qqm7-mfv7
(CVE-2025-14177) fixed the same leak in the chunked reader that newer
PHP versions use; on 5.6 this check is the fix.

The upstream test image (a 699-byte JPEG) is inlined in the test as
base64 and written to a temporary file: Portage applies user patches
with GNU patch, which cannot apply git binary diffs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ext/standard/image.c                   |  2 +-
 ext/standard/tests/image/bug71848.phpt | 51 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 ext/standard/tests/image/bug71848.phpt

diff --git a/ext/standard/image.c b/ext/standard/image.c
index d58d543a..f8e60659 100644
--- a/ext/standard/image.c
+++ b/ext/standard/image.c
@@ -440,7 +440,7 @@ static int php_read_APP(php_stream * stream, unsigned int marker, zval *info TSR
 
 	buffer = emalloc(length);
 
-	if (php_stream_read(stream, buffer, (long) length) <= 0) {
+	if (php_stream_read(stream, buffer, (long) length) != length) {
 		efree(buffer);
 		return 0;
 	}
diff --git a/ext/standard/tests/image/bug71848.phpt b/ext/standard/tests/image/bug71848.phpt
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..2a024201
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ext/standard/tests/image/bug71848.phpt
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
